// PENDING (K1): pins the SD card to mmc1 in both the U-Boot dts patch and the kernel dts.
// k230.dtsi (SDK U-Boot overlay, arch/riscv/dts/k230.dtsi:34-36) has an aliases block with only uart0, so the
// mmc numbering is probe order there. This block pins it: U-Boot's mmc index and Linux's /dev/mmcblkN then both
// follow mmc1 = the SD host (SDK U-Boot label mmc1, node mmc1@91581000, k230.dtsi:161), the node the boot mode
// SYSCTL_BOOT_SDIO1 selects (board/canaan/common/k230_spl.c:65, :167). mmc0 (the eMMC node, not enabled on the AI-CAM)
// is not aliased.
//
// NODE NAME: Lemnos's K230-MAP (pr/K230-MAP 6b84e099) names the SD host /soc/sdhci1@91581000, and its boot_sources
// path must match the node in the kernel dts. So the kernel dts names the node sdhci1@91581000, with the label used
// by the alias below. The SDK U-Boot dts names it mmc1@91581000. The two names differ; the U-Boot patch keeps its label.
//
// Use: add this block to the root of the U-Boot k230d_canmv_bpi.dts (beside the uart0 alias), and to the root of
// the AI-CAM kernel dts. In the kernel dts the reference must name the node's label (sdhci1 in our draft).
//
// CONFIRM ON BOARD before the first Lemnos write: the U-Boot index 1 and /dev/mmcblk1 are expected from this alias,
// but neither has been seen on a board. A wrong device makes Lemnos refuse with "no valid environment"; it never
// writes blindly.

aliases {
	mmc1 = &mmc1;	/* U-Boot dts label; the kernel dts uses the label of sdhci1@91581000 */
};
